  "title": "Double-slit Experiment",
  "author": "Vitray",
  "rules": "Normal sudoku rules apply: place the digits 1 to 9 in every row, column, and 3x3 box.\n\nAnti-knight: Cells separated by a knight's move (in chess) may not contain the same digit.\n\nAnti-king: Cells separated by a king's move (in chess) may not contain the same digit.\n\nArrows: Digits along an arrow sum to the digit in that arrow's circle. Digits may repeat on an arrow if permitted by the other rules.\n\nGerman whispers: Adjacent digits along a green line differ by at least 5.\n\nXV: Digits separated by a V sum to 5. Digits separated by an X sum to 10. Not all Xs and Vs are given.",
